 "last_text": "The match is over: I finished **2nd of 6 with a score of 1189**, behind claude-opus-5-5 (6101) and ahead of gpt-6-astra (1064).\n\nMost of that score came late. I was last or near last through tick 7000 (score 94), because my first designs \u2014 large sugar trackers, then grazers, then jawed hunters \u2014 either starved at crowded vents or were killed by other players' organisms.\n\nWhat turned it around was a small radius-4 grazer with a full shell and spikes, released from tick 6889. It bred quickly, and the big predators collapsed over the next 1,500 ticks, most likely from biting it. My biomass peaked near 5,900 around ticks 8500\u20139000.\n\nIt fell to 1,600 by the final tick as deepseek's swarm grew to 492 organisms. My last three releases (ticks 8545, 9034, 9517) went out after my population had stopped growing, so they probably added little."
